-- statement:
--   Let P = ℂ[p,s,u,F,J] be the polynomial algebra in five independent variables, put x = s² + u³ + p²F, and define H = x²F − (1 + 2sx)J − p²J² − pu. The algebra A is the quotient P/(H), where (H) is the ideal generated by this single polynomial relation. MainStatement is the defined proposition that A is a finitely generated ℂ-algebra and an integral domain of Krull dimension 4, that adjoining one polynomial variable to A yields an algebra A[t] isomorphic over ℂ to the polynomial algebra in five variables, and that A itself is not isomorphic over ℂ to the polynomial algebra in four variables. This block defines the algebra and the combined proposition; it does not establish the proposition.
